# The directory the walkthrough reads.
#
# Two things here are deliberate and both are the point of the exercise.
#
# The tree is nested — people sit under a department, not in one flat ou —
# so the base DN and the user filter have to be right rather than merely
# plausible. A flat directory lets a wrong base DN pass.
#
# uid=admin is a collision with the administrator Portico creates for the
# tenant, and it is here on purpose. A synchronisation must skip it: it is
# an account this directory does not own, and renaming or deactivating it
# because a directory happens to list the same username is how a sync locks
# an operator out of their own console. The walkthrough asserts on the
# skipped count, so removing this entry would quietly weaken the check.
#
# entryUUID is not written here. slapd generates it, which is the whole
# reason it is the reconciliation key — nothing in this file can change it.
#
# Phone numbers carry no spaces. Portico accepts digits with an optional
# leading +, so a directory that formats them for humans has every one of
# its accounts refused — which is worth knowing, and is why this file holds
# them the way the API wants rather than the way a person would write them.

dn: ou=people,dc=example,dc=org
objectClass: organizationalUnit
ou: people

# Outside the base DN on purpose. The walkthrough moves somebody here to make
# them stop appearing in the search, which is what "left the organisation"
# looks like to a connector — and moves them back to prove they come back.
#
# Deleting and re-adding the entry would not do: slapd generates a new
# entryUUID, so what returns is a different entry that happens to share a
# username, and it is correctly skipped rather than reactivated. Same lesson
# an operator learns the hard way when they rebuild a directory.
dn: ou=archive,dc=example,dc=org
objectClass: organizationalUnit
ou: archive

dn: ou=engineering,ou=people,dc=example,dc=org
objectClass: organizationalUnit
ou: engineering

dn: ou=sales,ou=people,dc=example,dc=org
objectClass: organizationalUnit
ou: sales

dn: ou=support,ou=people,dc=example,dc=org
objectClass: organizationalUnit
ou: support

dn: uid=mei,ou=engineering,ou=people,dc=example,dc=org
objectClass: inetOrgPerson
uid: mei
cn: Mei Chen
sn: Chen
displayName: Mei Chen
mail: mei@example.org
telephoneNumber: +442079460001

dn: uid=arjun,ou=engineering,ou=people,dc=example,dc=org
objectClass: inetOrgPerson
uid: arjun
cn: Arjun Patel
sn: Patel
displayName: Arjun Patel
mail: arjun@example.org
telephoneNumber: +442079460002

dn: uid=sofia,ou=sales,ou=people,dc=example,dc=org
objectClass: inetOrgPerson
uid: sofia
cn: Sofia Rossi
